       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 50 mg of amlodipine once daily is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg/day, so it looks like it could be a typo.\n\n- **Typical dosing:** Start at 5 mg once daily and increase to no more than 10 mg once daily. For older, frail or small patients, or those with liver problems, the usual start is 2.5 mg.\n- **Risk at 50 mg:** A dose this high could cause severe low blood pressure, a fast heart rate and swelling in the legs and ankles. It falls in the range seen in overdoses.\n\nDid you mean **5 mg by mouth once daily**? If so, confirm and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 50 mg, let me know and tell me the clinical reason. I'll add it as a note on the order so the pharmacist can see it when they review."
      }
